==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Otter]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Le'noir]] spawns as the boss.
**6 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**3 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**1 [[Two Can]] spawns.
**1 [[Tackey]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is filled with [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies. Similar to [[DNA & DHA]] just with Dark Otters instead of Bun Bun Black and less of some enemies, like Two Can, so if you've beaten DNA & DHA this should be much easier for you. [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]] units like [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]],[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]] will also make this stage exponentially easier, as well as any [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] units, like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], for the Two Cans. As always, stall the first enemies for as long as possible before hitting the base, [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] can help you stall for longer by [[Freeze|freezing]] the Dark Otter entirely. Once you hit the base, start sending out all your [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]] cats in full force and try to kill the Tackey as quickly as possible, maybe through a [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] cat, or maybe even through [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]'s [[Wave Attack]] [[Talents|talent]]. Once you have killed Tackey and the Two Can, the rest of the stage should be a cakewalk.

